                %li
                  %a{:href => "#transgression_in_group_cohomology"} Transgression in group cohomology
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            relates
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+abelian+groups"} simplicial abelian groups
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connective+chain+complexes"} connective chain complexes
            %em Eilenberg-Zilber theorem
            says how in this context
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complexes"} double complexes
            and their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complexes"} total complexes
            relate to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial groups
            and their
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+of+a+bisimplicial+set"} diagonals
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+simplicial+sets"} total simplicial sets
          %p Analogously there is also a version of the theorem for bi-cosimplicial abelian groups.
          %h2#statement Statement
          %h3#a_version_for_simplicial_abelian_groups A version for simplicial abelian groups:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \colon \Delta^{op} \times \Delta^{op} \to Ab
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+object"} bisimplicial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mo •
                      %mi diag
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet diag A
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                of its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+of+a+bisimplicial+set"} diagonal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+group"} simplicial group
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi diag
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                        %mi Ab
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} diag A \colon \Delta^{op} \to \Delta^{op} \times \Delta^{op} \stackrel{A}{\to} Ab
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Tot
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tot (C A)
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
                obtained by applying the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complex"} Moore complex
                functor on both arguments of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Dold-Puppe generalization of Eilenberg-Zilber)
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
              (even a chain-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"}> homotopy equivalence
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mi diag
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi Tot
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R : C_\bullet diag (A) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Tot C (A)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Notice (see the discussion at
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial set
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} realization
              given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi diag
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mo •
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Δ
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    diag F_{\bullet,\bullet}
                    \\simeq
                    \\int^{[n] \in \Delta} \Delta^n \times F_{n,\bullet}
                    \\,.
          %h3#cosimplicial_version Cosimplicial version
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A : \Delta \times \Delta \to Ab
            be a bi-cosimplicial abelian group. And let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Ab
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ch
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C : Ab^\Delta \to Ch^\bullet
            the Moore cochain complex functor. Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(A)
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+complex"} double complex
            obtained by applying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to each of the two cosimplicial directions. Then we have
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mi diag
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mi Tot
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^\bullet C^\bullet diag(A)
                    \\simeq
                    H^\bullet Tot C^\bullet(A)
          %h3#crossed_complex_version Crossed complex version
          %p
            A version for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complexes"} crossed complexes
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andy+Tonks"} Andy Tonks
          %p
            First note that there is a tensor product for crossed complexes developed by Brown and Higgins. Letting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            be simplicial sets.
          %ul
            %li There is an Alexander-Whitney diagonal approximation defined as a natural transformation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ,
                      %mi L
                  %mo :
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo ×
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi π
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi π
                  %mi L
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{K,L}: \pi(K\times L)\to \pi K \otimes \pi L.
          %ul
            %li
              Using
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shuffles"} shuffles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ,
                      %mi L
                  %mo :
                  %mi π
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi π
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo ×
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_{K,L}:\pi K \otimes \pi L \to\pi(K\times L),
          %p in a somewhat similar way to chain complexes.
          %ul
            %li The composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo ×
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi π
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi π
                  %mi L
                  %mo →
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo ×
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(K\times L)\to \pi K \otimes \pi L\to\pi(K\times L),
          %p
            is homotopic to the identity on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ×
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(K\times L)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi π
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi K \otimes \pi L
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ×
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi(K\times L)
          %h3#the_eilenberg__zilber_theorem_for_simplicial_sets The Eilenberg - Zilber theorem for simplicial sets
          %p
            Cegarra and Remedios have proved a version of the Eilenberg - Zilber theorem for simplicial sets. This is discussed under the entry on
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial set
          %h2#applications Applications
          %h3#eilenbergzilberalexanderwhitney_deformation_retraction Eilenberg-Zilber/Alexander-Whitney deformation retraction
          %p
          #EZAWDeformationRetract.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber%2FAlexander-Whitney+deformation+retraction"}> Eilenberg-Zilber/Alexander-Whitney deformation retraction
                )
              %br/
            %p Let
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi sAb
                      %mo =
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B \,\in\, sAb =
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SimplicialAbelianGroups"} SimplicialAbelianGroups
            %p and denote
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ch
                          %mo •
                          %mo +
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(A), N(B) \,\in\, Ch^+_\bullet =
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ConnectiveChainComplexes"} ConnectiveChainComplexes
                  their
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chain+complexes"} normalized chain complexes
              %li
                %p
                  by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi B
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi sAb
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B \,\in\, sAb
                  the degreewise
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              %li
                %p
                  by
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(A) \otimes N(B)
                  the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
            %p
              Then there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retraction"} deformation retraction
