            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+retraction"} deformation retraction
            for normalized chain complexes is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "EZAW+deformation+retraction#EilenbergMacLane54"} Eilenberg &amp; MacLane 1954, Thm. 2.1a
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "EZAW+deformation+retraction#May67"} May 1967, Cor. 29.10
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+operator"} homotopy operator
            is given in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "EZAW+deformation+retraction#GonzalezDiazReal99"} Gonzalez-Diaz &amp; Real 1999
          %h3#ProdTopSp Homology of products of topological spaces
          %p
            The following is the special case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Zilber%2FAlexander-Whitney+deformation+retraction"} Eilenberg-Zilber/Alexander-Whitney deformation retraction
            (Prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EZAWDeformationRetract"}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+sets"} singular simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+simplicial+abelian+groups"} free simplicial abelian groups
            preserves monoidal products. This is the original motivating application in
            %a{:href => "#EilenbergZilber53"} Eilenberg &amp;Zilber 1953
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            be two
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(X)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(Y)
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moore+complexes"} Moore complexes
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+abelian+groups"} simplicial abelian groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[Sing X]
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[Sing Y]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
            on their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complexes"} singular simplicial complexes
          %p
            So from the Dold-Puppe
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
